    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6684" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Capsa</span></b> , ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in Africa</i>,
				<i>in the districl of Byzacium</i>, <i>surrounded by vast deserts</i>, <i>plundered by Marius in the Jugurthine war</i>, <i><span class="en">Sall. J.
				89, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">91</span></i>
			sq.; <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 1, 14</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Capsenses</span></b> , ium,
				m., <i>the inhabitants of Capsa</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Sall. J. 92, 3 sq.</span></i>; in <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 4,
				4, § 30</span></i>, called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Capsĭtāni</span></b> .</div>
